---
layout: changelog
title: "Sign users in with Vipps MobilePay in Appwrite Auth"
date: 2026-11-11
cover: /images/blog/announcing-vipps-mobilepay-login/cover.avif
tags: auth, integrations
---

Appwrite Auth now supports [Vipps MobilePay](/integrations/oauth-vipps-mobilepay) as an OAuth2 login provider. Users in Norway and Sweden sign in with the Vipps app, and users in Denmark and Finland with MobilePay, through one provider.

There are two providers. **Vipps MobilePay** (`OAuthProvider.Vipps`) uses the production environment, and **Vipps MobilePay Sandbox** (`OAuthProvider.VippsSandbox`) uses the Vipps MobilePay test environment, so you can build and test with a test sales unit before your production keys arrive. Appwrite stores the user's name and email, and marks the email as verified only when Vipps MobilePay reports it as verified.

Enable either provider in the Console under **Auth** > **Social providers** with the `client_id` and `client_secret` from your sales unit. Both are live on Appwrite Cloud and ship in the next self-hosted release.

